secureshellgo (1.3.0~noble1) noble; urgency=medium

  * Desktop workspace: split the terminal area into up to four resizable
    panes each showing a different server, with broadcast input across
    every visible pane, server groups with colour tags, a Ctrl+K command
    palette, a quick-connect bar, ~/.ssh/config import, command snippets
    and per-host startup commands.
  * Connections: automatic reconnection with keep-alive, jump hosts
    (ProxyJump) with both hops verified, and a tunnel manager for local,
    remote and dynamic SOCKS5 forwards.
  * Files: a built-in remote editor with syntax highlighting for thirteen
    languages and a stat-guarded temp-then-rename save, path bookmarks,
    and one transfer panel across every session.
  * Monitoring: server stats, a live log viewer, and a systemd service and
    process manager.
  * Security: optional app lock, an encrypted backup format (Argon2id and
    AES-256-GCM), in-app ed25519 key generation and installation, and a
    known-hosts manager.
  * Fixes the desktop icon regression from ~noble8 as 1.2.1 did, and two
    faults found by driving the built application against a real server:
    ordinary sessions no longer request SSH agent forwarding, which had
    made every exec-based feature fail after the first command, and the
    server-stats probe no longer collapses into a shell comment.

 -- Dhiva Labs <dhivakar1010@gmail.com>  Thu, 31 Jul 2026 22:30:00 +0530

secureshellgo (1.2.1~noble1) noble; urgency=medium

  * Fix the running app showing the generic gear icon in the GNOME dock.
    GNOME Shell matches a Wayland window to its launcher by looking up
    <application-id>.desktop; the packaged entry was named
    secureshellgo.desktop while the app identifies itself as
    com.dhivalabs.secure_shell_go, so the running window never matched
    and fell back to the generic executable icon. Rename the installed
    desktop entry to com.dhivalabs.secure_shell_go.desktop and point
    StartupWMClass at the real WM_CLASS (the runner sets prgname to the
    application id, verified with xprop) so X11 sessions match as well.

 -- Dhiva Labs <dhivakar1010@gmail.com>  Fri, 31 Jul 2026 14:20:00 +0530

secureshellgo (1.2.0~noble8) noble; urgency=medium

  * The ~noble7 rootUri rewrite made every package share one root, and
    the Dart VM rejects a package_config with duplicate roots when it
    loads the file during the build — caught by the pristine local
    rehearsal before upload. Rewrite instead points each entry at its
    own generated stub directory (pubstubs/<name>/ with a real
    pubspec.yaml), keeping the file parse-valid for the VM and
    existence-valid for flutter_tools' staleness probe. Declares
    python3 in Build-Depends for the rewrite.

 -- Dhiva Labs <dhivakar1010@gmail.com>  Fri, 31 Jul 2026 13:55:00 +0530

secureshellgo (1.2.0~noble7) noble; urgency=medium

  * Root cause of every offline-resolution failure since ~noble2, found
    via the ~noble6 diagnostic build: the vendored SDK ships flutter_
    tools/.dart_tool/package_config.json with absolute rootUris into
    the scratch pub cache of the machine that produced the tarball.
    flutter_tools' PubDependencies.isUpToDate validates those paths
    exist; on any other machine they do not, the artifact reads as
    stale, and the tool re-resolves its own package ONLINE (ignoring
    our --offline), asking pub.dev for its dev dependency `test`.
    Rewrite every rootUri to point at flutter_tools itself before the
    build — the probe validates only that a pubspec.yaml exists, and
    the tool runs from its AOT snapshot rather than this file.

 -- Dhiva Labs <dhivakar1010@gmail.com>  Fri, 31 Jul 2026 13:20:00 +0530

secureshellgo (1.2.0~noble6) noble; urgency=medium

  * Diagnostic build. Local network-isolated replicas of the ~noble5
    source package (sanitized environment, tilde directory name,
    HOME=/sbuild-nonexistent, zero network) build to completion, while
    the Launchpad builder fails at `flutter pub get --offline` asking
